      "response": "\n\nMinami set his tray down and looked at Arro over the rim of his soup cup. \"You've scheduled three 'casual hangouts' for me this week,\" he said, voice even. \"I'm not a calendar entry you're trying to fill.\"\n\nArro blinked. The cafeteria hum around them felt suddenly loud. He hadn't realized he'd been doing it out loud, arranging introductions like supply drops. \"I thought\u2014 I mean, you mentioned wanting to meet people.\"\n\n\"I did,\" Minami agreed. \"I didn't mention letting you vet them first.\" He picked up his chopsticks again, not unkindly. \"Next time, just ask if I want company. Don't build a plan around my back.\"\n\nArro nodded slowly, feeling the shape of his own habit press against him. It wasn't malice, just momentum\u2014the same way he'd organized study schedules and shared notes without asking. But Minami wasn't a problem to be solved. He was a friend who had already told him what he wanted, and Arro had kept steering anyway.\n\n\"Okay,\" Arro said. \"No more plans. Just... let me know if you need a ride somewhere.\"\n\nMinami's mouth twitched, almost a smile. \"Deal.\"",
